Description: Fix FTBFS with clang 17 ("type constraint differs in template redeclaration")
 clang 17 (the compiler shipped by deepin) rejects the out-of-line definition of
 CSS::PrimitiveNumericOrKeyword when the enclosing class template PrimitiveNumeric
 has already been instantiated before that definition is seen, which is what happens
 in unified builds:
 .
   CSSPrimitiveNumericOrKeyword.h:34:10: error: type constraint differs in template redeclaration
   CSSPrimitiveNumeric.h:155:14: note: previous template declaration is here
 .
 Forward declare CSS::PrimitiveNumericOrKeyword before PrimitiveNumeric, so the
 constrained friend declaration refers to an already declared template. This mirrors
 what WebCore::Style::PrimitiveNumeric already does for its own constrained friend
 declaration (StylePrimitiveNumeric.h), and it does not change any behaviour.
Origin: vendor, https://github.com/deepin-community/wpewebkit/pull/9
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-27
Author: lichenggang <lichenggang@uniontech.com>
---
diff --git a/Source/WebCore/css/values/primitives/CSSPrimitiveNumeric.h b/Source/WebCore/css/values/primitives/CSSPrimitiveNumeric.h
index 1cad6114..6ca4166d 100644
--- a/Source/WebCore/css/values/primitives/CSSPrimitiveNumeric.h
+++ b/Source/WebCore/css/values/primitives/CSSPrimitiveNumeric.h
@@ -43,6 +43,14 @@ namespace CSS {
 // the CSS value gets resolved to. Unresolved CSS primitive numeric types always use a `double` as
 // its internal representation.
 
+// NOTE: This forward declaration is needed so that the constrained friend declaration of
+// `PrimitiveNumericOrKeyword` inside `PrimitiveNumeric` below refers to an already declared
+// template. Without it, clang (at least clang 17, which is what ships with some distros) rejects
+// the definition of `PrimitiveNumericOrKeyword` with "type constraint differs in template
+// redeclaration" whenever `PrimitiveNumeric` has already been instantiated before that definition
+// is seen, which is what happens in unified builds.
+template<Numeric, SpecificKeyword...> struct PrimitiveNumericOrKeyword;
+
 template<NumericRaw RawType> struct PrimitiveNumeric {
     using Raw = RawType;
     using Calc = UnevaluatedCalc<Raw>;
